A bird model gets 98 of 100 training photos right, but only 60 of 100 separate validation photos right. This code compares those recorded counts.

```javascript
const trainingCorrect = 98;
const validationCorrect = 60;
const gap = trainingCorrect - validationCorrect;
console.log(gap);
```

It prints 38. The large gap is a reason to investigate; the code does not train the model or prove the cause.
